WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.867
Lawmakers from both

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.568
sides of the aisle

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.403
commemorated International Holocaust

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.171
Remembrance Day on Friday,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.107
including this one.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.575
I would like to take a moment

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.175
to acknowledge

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.843
a grandmother

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.511
of one of my deceased staffers

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.214
who the 93 year old survivor of Auschwitz

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.148
and is also

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.017
one of the few survivors of her family

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.418
who was tragically

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.787
lost at the hands of Nazi murders.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.590
anti-Semitism is a plague in this nation,

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.825
and it is undoubtedly up to us

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:26.326
to ensure

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.460
this kind of tragedy

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.163
is never to be seen again.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.166
So just as a reminder, George Santos

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.035
lied about being Jewish.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.202
And not only that,

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.872
he also lied about his grandparents

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.641
escaping the Holocaust.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.710
I've seen how socialism destroys

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.011
people's lives

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.179
because my grandparents

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.747
survived the Holocaust.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.648
For a lot of people

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.283
who are descendants of World

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.818
War Two refugees

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.753
or survivors of the Holocaust,

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.889
a lot of names and paperwork were changed

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.257
and in name of survival.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.792
So I don't carry the family.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.293
Last name that would have been

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.161
the BRAF scheme

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.298
That is.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.399
It's amazing.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.801
But but it's it's

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:12.238
just in the context of this very sober

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.006
and somber

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.108
moment of Holocaust remembrance.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.944
I mean, there's no shame.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:18.645
Exactly.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.480
I actually had in my office

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.414
the House floor

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.551
camera up and I was not alerted

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.518
that he was going to take the floor.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.553
And all of a sudden I was like,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.388
oh, no, he's not going to really do this

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.289
right now.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:32.025
He's just trolling us at this point.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.128
So, yes, no shame is one thing here.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:35.528
But

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.998
for all the distraction

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.633
that is George Santos,

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.236
I do think the campaign finance piece of

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.171
this is the piece

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.339
we should keep our eyes on

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.740
because it is clear

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.608
Kevin McCarthy

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.610
and House Republicans

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.377
are not interested

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.446
in doing anything about Santos.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.215
But if indeed

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.749
there is a criminal investigation

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.383
into his campaign

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.319
finances that emerges with an indictment

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.187
that will change the calculus, that will

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.088
all of a sudden

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:02.956
that will change

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.591
Kevin McCarthy's behavior.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.191
One would imagine

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.392
as it relates to George Senator to.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.161
So I would keep our eyes on

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.596
what's happening with his finances.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:10.663
It's pretty much the only thing

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.798
that might change the calculus,

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.233
because the unwillingness,

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:13.967
particularly on the House

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.768
Republican side, is so high.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.370
I mean, this Jorge Santos,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.838
I mean, the audacity is kind

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.473
of stunning on every level.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.107
And to your point

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.942
about the shamelessness of this act.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:23.409
But I think

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.711
also we see someone

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.213
who is reveling in their newfound fame.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.381
I think it speaks to

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.782
a new type of Congress

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:30.850
we have on our hands

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.484
where we think

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.253
that there are some figures

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:33.653
who are there

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.522
for the serious business of legislating,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.289
but there are other figures

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:36.656
who are there

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.191
for the very unserious business of

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.592
just trying to become a celebrity.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:39.859
Well, here's

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.694
the thing about being on Capitol Hill.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.863
You're not going to escape the reporter's

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.165
entourage.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.566
You doing the Lord's

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.634
work, trying to get some

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.102
answers out of Jorge Santos

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.105
why did you amend your

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.407
FEC reports to say 500?

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.575
Let's make it very clear.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:56.543
I don't amend anything.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:59.045
I don't touch any of my FEC stuff. Right.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.346
So don't be disingenuous

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.281
and report that I did,

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:01.881
because you know

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.551
that every campaign hires a fiduciary.

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.553
So I'm not aware of that answer.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:07.921
And we'll have an answer for the press

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.656
regarding the amendment from yesterday

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.356
when it was

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:10.623
the one

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.225
was the source of your funds, sir.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.726
What was the source of that money?

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:13.893
Mr.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.327
Sanders,

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.262
you listed the wrong name of a treasurer.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.497
Why did you list the wrong name

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.631
of your treasurer

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:21.034
and your campaign finance forms?

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.335
I'll have the conversation with you.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:22.468
What?

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.103
You become a better honest reporter.

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.705
I'm asking you directly.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:26.906
Reporter No, that

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.375
Now, this is

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.210
all good and

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.411
and fine

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.213
until the feds come calling, right?

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.413
Yeah.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.480
And a Department of Justice

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.281
investigation, right?

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.382
Writing the FEC, looking in this.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:36.950
I mean, they think that

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.985
that totally changes the calculation.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.787
I think that everything we've seen

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:44.324
to date has been relatively disingenuous.

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:45.358
But I would also argue

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.793
that we've entered an era of politics

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.860
where a lot of politicians lie

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:48.561
about things.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.028
That being said,

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:49.896
you actually Donald Trump

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.030
was it yesterday saying

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.065
that George Santos told

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:52.832
a lot of whoppers.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.033
And so when you have

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.101
the former president,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.437
who was known not to be the most honest

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.440
calling you out for your level of honesty

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:01.874
there, does perhaps

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.042
elevate that situation.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:03.910
But I agree with everyone here

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.344
at this table.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.578
I don't think it changes

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.413
nothing changes a calculation for House

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.648
Republican leadership

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.383
unless there's an actual investigation.

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:10.650
Yeah.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.252
And this is all despite the fact

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.087
that according to a new poll

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.288
out this week,

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:18.091
his constituents want him to go at 64%

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:21.728
of Democrats, 49% of Republicans and 59%

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.263
of independents.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.331
New York state voters say

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.567
he should resign. Meanwhile,

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:29.902
Alex, just listen.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:30.203
This is

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.004
Kevin McCarthy

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.840
responding to questions

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.341
about why he won't do something,

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:36.709
really anything

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.578
to try to at least cordoned off

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.646
Jorge Santos

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.314
from being a member in good

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:44.250
standing in the House of Representatives.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.119
I try to stick by the Constitution.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.221
The voters elected him to serve.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.455
If there is a concern

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.923
and he has to go through the ethics,

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.525
let him move through that.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.793
The voters of his district

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.961
have elected him.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.162
He is seated.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.331
He is part of the Republican conference.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.266
You know, I'm standing by him

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:03.503
because his constituents voted for him.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:04.570
And as former Speaker

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.606
Paul Ryan put it just a few weeks ago,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.241
he was elected,

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.576
but based on a fraudulent candidacy,

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.544
it seems.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:11.778
Look,

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:14.213
I think it's not totally indefensible

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:14.881
as an argument

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:15.281
to say

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.382
the guy got elected

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:16.783
and I don't

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.685
particularly want him to be elected.

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:19.719
But here we are.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.553
And so

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:21.487
let him participate

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:22.522
in the business of the body.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.257
It's very hard to make that argument

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.024
in the convincing way

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.492
when you're also trying to kick Ilhan

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.828
Omar off the Foreign Affairs Committee

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.930
because you object to elements of her,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:31.764
her worldview.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:31.998
Right.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.032
That she was also elected

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.635
by her constituents in Minneapolis.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.569
And so if you

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.705
if you take the view generally that,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:39.272
you know,

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:39.839
the voters

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.240
are the ultimate arbiters of all this

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.442
and we have to be deferential to them,

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.643
you need to sort of stick to that.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:44.077
I will say

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.778
this is totally characteristic

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:46.646
of Kevin McCarthy

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.281
to make decisions

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.382
based on the most short

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.850
term calculus possible

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.784
and then make a different set

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:52.452
of decisions

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.020
whenever that calculus changes.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.088
But look,

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:56.322
he needs that vote right now

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.390
or he thinks he needs that vote

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:57.690
right now.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.925
He doesn't want a special election

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:00.927
on Long Island under these circumstances.

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:02.128
But the problem is,

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:03.129
you are going to need

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:05.465
to win that seat again in two years.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.300
One way or another.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.502
And if George Santos just four strings

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.204
you along until he actually winds up

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.238
running for reelection,

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:13.206
that's a bigger headache.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.274
Or if the voters of that district

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.743
see you and your party

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.977
as coddling this guy

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:18.644
who is just an

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:21.581
unbelievably offensive character, then

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.249
even if he doesn't run for reelection,

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.617
good luck to your next candidate.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:24.917
Yeah.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.819
And I mean, his colleagues

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:28.054
among New York Republicans

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.489
are basically making that argument.

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:30.356
They're like,

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:31.891
we need this guy gone

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.760
because he's hurting all of us.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.294
But also, we should note

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:36.896
he is

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:37.296
on Capitol

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.598
Hill trying to make friends,

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.633
having a bit of a tough time

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.834
because other members

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:42.301
kind of don't

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.437
want to be associated with him

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.906
because I think everybody recognizes

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.674
that they could be kind of tarnished

00:06:48.674 --> 00:06:50.843
by an association with someone who,

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.545
frankly, they don't even know who he is.

